# Who approves what. GitHub requires a review from every owner matched by a
# changed path; the LAST matching pattern wins, so order here is meaningful:
# broad defaults first, narrow territory last.
#
# !! PLACEHOLDER TEAM SLUGS !!
# The three slugs below are placeholders — no GitHub team by these names is
# guaranteed to exist yet. Before this file has any effect, either create the
# teams under the `osxsystem` org or rename them here (and, in the same change,
# in the `owner:` field of every entry in `.fork/catalog.yaml`, which mirrors
# this file):
#
#   @osxsystem/maintainers   fork maintainers — sync-aware review
#   @osxsystem/mobile        the mobile domain's discipline team
#   @osxsystem/platform      the platform domain's discipline team
#
# A slug that names no team means GitHub requests no review at all — the rule
# fails open, so a rename that misses one line silently unowns that path.

# Default: anything not claimed below is a maintainers call.
*                                   @osxsystem/maintainers

# --- Upstream territory (byte-frozen vendor files) --------------------------
# Edits here are boundary changes, not content changes: every one of them has
# to be sanctioned in `.fork/sanctioned-edits.txt` and survive a sync. Reviewed
# by maintainers, who carry the sync context — see `.fork/sync-playbook.md`.
/skills/engineering/                @osxsystem/maintainers
/skills/productivity/               @osxsystem/maintainers
/skills/misc/                       @osxsystem/maintainers
/skills/in-progress/                @osxsystem/maintainers
/skills/deprecated/                 @osxsystem/maintainers
/docs/engineering/                  @osxsystem/maintainers
/docs/productivity/                 @osxsystem/maintainers

# --- Fork control plane, harness, and CI ------------------------------------
/.fork/                             @osxsystem/maintainers
/scripts/                           @osxsystem/maintainers
/.github/                           @osxsystem/maintainers

# --- Team domains -----------------------------------------------------------
# One block per existing domain under `skills/team/`: the skills and the docs
# tree that mirrors them. A new domain folder adds a block here, a matching
# `owner:` in `.fork/catalog.yaml`, and nothing else.
/skills/team/mobile/                @osxsystem/mobile
/docs/team/mobile/                  @osxsystem/mobile

/skills/team/platform/              @osxsystem/platform
/docs/team/platform/                @osxsystem/platform
